Tesseract reads on one thread unless the caller sets OMP_THREAD_LIMIT (passed through to it).
Its OpenMP threads spin while they wait, so several readings at once (two documents read together)
each taking every core slowed each other to a standstill: four pages read together took more than
two minutes instead of 1.3 s with one thread each; a page alone reads as fast on one thread.

